# UDP Echo Client-Server in C

A simple UDP Echo Client-Server application developed in C using Linux Socket Programming APIs.

---

## 📌 Features

- UDP Server
- UDP Client
- IPv4 Socket Programming
- Echo Communication
- Blocking I/O
- Error Handling
- Wireshark Packet Analysis

---

## 🛠 Technologies Used

- C Programming
- Linux Socket API
- UDP Protocol
- IPv4
- Wireshark
- GCC Compiler

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```
UDP-Echo-Client-Server
│
├── src
│   ├── udp_server.c
│   └── udp_client.c
│
├── README.md
└── Makefile
```

---

## Socket APIs Used

- socket()
- bind()
- sendto()
- recvfrom()
- close()
- inet_pton()
- inet_ntoa()
- htons()
- ntohs()

---

## Build

```bash
gcc src/udp_server.c -o udp_server
gcc src/udp_client.c -o udp_client
```

---

## Run

### Terminal 1

```bash
./udp_server
```

### Terminal 2

```bash
./udp_client
```

---

## Example Output

### Server

```
Socket created successfully
Client IP : 127.0.0.1
Client Port : 51965
Received Message : Hello Sonal
```

### Client

```
Enter Message :
Hello Sonal

Message Sent Successfully
Echo from Server : Hello Sonal
```

---

## Packet Flow

```
Client
   |
sendto()
   |
   v
Kernel
   |
UDP Packet
   |
Loopback Interface
   |
recvfrom()
   |
Server
   |
sendto()
   |
Client
```

---

## Wireshark Verification

The application was verified using Wireshark.

Observed:

- Source IP : 127.0.0.1
- Destination IP : 127.0.0.1
- Source Port : Ephemeral Port
- Destination Port : 5000
- UDP Payload : Hello Sonal

